Implemented in `app/page.tsx:1` as an async Server Component using Next.js’s recommended `connection()` API:

```tsx
import { connection } from "next/server";

export default async function Home() {
  await connection();
  const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Server Timestamp</h1>
      <p>{timestamp}</p>
    </main>
  );
}
```

Why this matches your requirement:
- `await connection()` opts the route out of static prerendering at build time.
- `new Date().toISOString()` runs at request time, so it changes on each page load.
- This follows the local Next.js docs recommendation for dynamic rendering without relying on `cookies()`/`headers()`.
